IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `il-interpretation-law`

-- Israel: Law s 1's gate, as a helper for the rules of reading and the scope-of-power rules.
--
-- Law s 1 says the Law applies "if there is no other provision on the matter and if there is nothing in the matter
-- or its context inconsistent with this Law". `s 1 — the Law governs` (il-interpretation-law.l4) is that test over
-- the two judgements the caller makes. This module adds what the rules of reading do when the test fails: the Law
-- does not say what the words mean in that case, and so the rule REFUSES; it does not answer FALSE, which would
-- read as "the singular does not include the plural here".
-- Sources: the unofficial Wikisource consolidations, ../../source/law.wiki (src:N).

§ `Interpretation Law s 1: the gate, as a helper`

-- src:22 | חוק זה יחול לגבי כל חיקוק והוראת מינהל, אף אם ניתנו לפני תחילתו, אם אין הוראה אחרת לענין הנדון ואם אין בענין הנדון או בהקשרו דבר שאינו מתיישב עם חוק זה; אולם על מלים וביטויים למעט ”חטא“, ”עוון“ ו”פשע“, שבחיקוקים והוראות מינהל שניתנו לפני תחילת חוק זה לא יחול
-- src:22 | סעיף 3 אלא יוסיפו לחול ההגדרות
-- src:22 | שבסעיף 1 לפקודת הפרשנות.
@ref Interpretation Law s 1 (src:22)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the Law is displaced here: another provision deals with the matter, or the matter or its context is inconsistent with the Law, so the Law does not say what the words mean` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Law is displaced here: another provision deals with the matter, or the matter or its context is inconsistent with the Law, so the Law does not say what the words mean"

-- Gives the Law's answer when s 1 lets the Law govern the matter, and the named refusal when it does not.
-- The answer is not evaluated unless the gate is open.
@ref Interpretation Law s 1 (src:22)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
      matter IS A `The matter in question`
      answer IS AN a
GIVETH AN a
`under s 1, the Law's answer for` matter `is` answer MEANS
    IF   `s 1 — the Law governs` matter
    THEN answer
    ELSE `the Law is displaced here: another provision deals with the matter, or the matter or its context is inconsistent with the Law, so the Law does not say what the words mean`

§§ `Illustrations`

`a matter nothing displaces` MEANS `The matter in question` WITH
    `another provision deals with it` IS FALSE
    `something in it or its context is inconsistent with the Law` IS FALSE

`a matter another provision deals with` MEANS `The matter in question` WITH
    `another provision deals with it` IS TRUE
    `something in it or its context is inconsistent with the Law` IS FALSE

`a matter whose context is inconsistent with the Law` MEANS `The matter in question` WITH
    `another provision deals with it` IS FALSE
    `something in it or its context is inconsistent with the Law` IS TRUE

§§ `Which sections reach which instruments, by date and by kind`

-- Law s 1 applies the Law "to every enactment and administrative direction, even if given before its commencement". The kind of
-- instrument is therefore what decides whether sections 2 and 4 to 26 reach it, and its date does not. Section 3 is the exception
-- for words: for an enactment given before the Law it reaches only sin, misdemeanour and felony (pass 1's `s 1 — section 3 applies to`
-- answers that word by word), so this function refuses for section 3 and an earlier enactment. A private contract and any other
-- document are not named by s 1, so the Law's rules do not reach them by s 1: FALSE means "s 1 does not extend to it", not "the Law says no".
DECLARE `A kind of instrument` IS ONE OF
    `the instrument is an enactment`
    `the instrument is an administrative direction`
    `the instrument is a private contract`
    `the instrument is some other document`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`s 3 reaches the words of an enactment given before the Law only for sin, misdemeanour and felony, so the answer turns on the word` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 3 reaches the words of an enactment given before the Law only for sin, misdemeanour and felony; for every other word the Ordinance's definitions continue to govern, so the answer turns on the word"

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`s 1 applies the rules of interpretation of sections 2 to 26; the other sections say how the Law begins, what it repeals and where the text was merged` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 1 applies the rules of interpretation of sections 2 to 26 to enactments and administrative directions; sections 1 and 27 to 33 say how the Law applies, what it repeals and where its text was merged, and are not rules that s 1 applies"

-- src:22 | חוק זה יחול לגבי כל חיקוק והוראת מינהל, אף אם ניתנו לפני תחילתו, אם אין הוראה אחרת לענין הנדון ואם אין בענין הנדון או בהקשרו דבר שאינו מתיישב עם חוק זה; אולם על מלים וביטויים למעט ”חטא“, ”עוון“ ו”פשע“, שבחיקוקים והוראות מינהל שניתנו לפני תחילת חוק זה לא יחול
-- src:22 | סעיף 3 אלא יוסיפו לחול ההגדרות
-- src:22 | שבסעיף 1 לפקודת הפרשנות.
@ref Interpretation Law s 1 (src:22)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      kind IS A `A kind of instrument`
      d IS A DATE
      matter IS A `The matter in question`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1 — section` n `of the Law reaches an instrument of the kind` kind `given on` d `, for` matter MEANS
    `under s 1, the Law's answer for` matter `is`
        (IF   n EQUALS 3
         THEN IF   `s 1 — it was before the Law commenced that an enactment was given on` d
              THEN `s 3 reaches the words of an enactment given before the Law only for sin, misdemeanour and felony, so the answer turns on the word`
              ELSE reach
         ELSE IF   n EQUALS 2 OR (n AT LEAST 4 AND n AT MOST 26)
              THEN reach
              ELSE `s 1 applies the rules of interpretation of sections 2 to 26; the other sections say how the Law begins, what it repeals and where the text was merged`)
    WHERE
        reach MEANS
            CONSIDER kind
            WHEN `the instrument is an enactment`                THEN TRUE
            WHEN `the instrument is an administrative direction` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `the instrument is a private contract`          THEN FALSE
            WHEN `the instrument is some other document`         THEN FALSE
